//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu1, chess
//
// TODO: move to Peano. kernel.cpp pins its probe variable at the tile-mapped
// base with chess_storage(TM : 0x80000) so it can read the lock registers.
// Peano defines chess_storage(...) as an empty macro (aiebase_chess.h), so the
// address is silently dropped, the variable lands wherever the linker puts it,
// and the test reads unrelated memory. Note this FAILS AT RUNTIME rather than
// at build time: it compiles and links clean and returns wrong data, so a
// Peano port of this test needs an absolute-placement mechanism first (section
// attribute plus a linker script) and must be checked on device, not by
// building it.
//
// RUN: xchesscc_wrapper aie2 -I %aietools/include -c %S/kernel.cpp -o kernel.o
// RUN: %aiecc --xchesscc --xbridge --get-xclbin --get-npu-insts --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin %S/aie.mlir
// RUN: %host_clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags %host_link_flags %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
